Read class annotations in configclass through annotationlib on Python 3.14.

Python 3.14 evaluates annotations lazily (PEP 649), so they are no longer stored
in cls.__dict__["__annotations__"]. configclass read that dictionary directly,
so on 3.14 every class without `from __future__ import annotations` reported no
annotations and failed with "number of annotations (0) does not match number of
class members". Importing isaaclab.sim.schemas.schemas_cfg, and therefore the
`isaaclab train` CLI, failed at import time.

Add an _own_annotations() helper that uses annotationlib.get_annotations() with
the FORWARDREF format on 3.14, keeping unresolved forward references like the
previous behavior, and falls back to the class dictionary on older versions.
Instances no longer expose __annotations__ on 3.14, so the test reads it from
the class. Upstreamable as-is.
